/// `exact-distributions`: Finite distributions with exact weights.
/// Implemented: a distribution holds exact rational weights in one canonical order. `distributes` states the exact distribution of a definition's runs over every answer of its draws. A forked task and a `migrate` body draw as the root does, and a declined draw is refused by name.
/// Not implemented: std carries no PRNG, universal hashing or one-time pad, each with its exact distribution.
///
/// - owes: #5713
/// - see: #6118
// One draw of one fair bit gives 0 and 1, each with weight one half. The
// corpus runs `bit` twice, once for each answer of its draw. The model
// source `draws.gandr` sums two draws of two bits.
//
// - see: `../../model/probability/draws.gandr`

// The host interface of randomness.
import std.rand;

/// One draw of one bit: 0 and 1, each with weight one half.
@[ distributes(("1/2 0", "1/2 1")) ]
def bit() -> [std.rand.Eff] Integer =
  std.rand.draw 1
